      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p><strong>Statutory Transit Paperwork &amp; Risk Coverage for Packers &amp; Movers Chennai to Jaipur</strong></p>

<p>When you choose a <em>packers and movers Jaipur to Chennai</em> service, the journey isn’t just about packing boxes; it involves a chain of legal documents and insurance that safeguard your belongings from the moment they leave your doorstep to the moment they arrive in the new city.</p>

<h3>GST e‑Way Bill</h3>
<p>Every interstate move in India requires a <strong>GST e‑Way Bill</strong> that authorises the transport of goods. The bill is generated electronically, linked to the shipment’s value, and must be presented at every checkpoint. It ensures compliance with the Goods and Services Tax regime and provides a trail for any audit.</p>

<h3>IBA‑Approved Lorry Receipts (LR/Bilty)</h3>
<p>Transporters issue an <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt</strong>, also known as a <strong>LR or Bilty</strong>. This document records the cargo details, the carrier’s identification, and the agreed freight charges. It is the primary contract between the shipper and the carrier and is mandatory for all interstate freight.</p>

<h3>IRDAI Marine Transit Insurance</h3>
<p>To protect against accidental collision, theft, or unforeseen delays, a <strong>100% declared‑value IRDAI marine transit insurance</strong> is recommended. This coverage covers:</p>
